{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"Now I understand the full picture. Let me analyze the current best method (round 9, raw=0.4628) and think about further optimizations.\n\nKey observation from round 10: in-place operations on `logits` caused numerical issues. Let me be careful.\n\nLet me think about what else can be optimized:\n\n1. **Current state**: v-first ordering (compute v first, apply attention to v), Gram-matrix norms, p_mix via lerp, combined projections.\n\n2. **Potential optimizations**:\n   - The Gram matrix G is `(B, L, L)` — can we share it across heads? Yes, it's already done (unsqueeze on dim 1).\n   - The `p1 @ G_exp` and `p_mix @ G_exp` are both `(B, H, L, L) @ (B, 1, L, L)` = `(B, H, L, L)` which is expensive.\n   - Wait, can we avoid computing `p_mix @ G` entirely? Since `p_mix = (1-beta)*p0 + beta*p1`, we have `||m||^2 = diag(p_mix @ G @ p_mix^T)`. Let's compute it from `p0@G`, `p1@G`, and cross terms.\n\nActually, from round 9's method summary it says \"we can compute normm_sq from p0, p1 and their cross, saving one large p@G multiplication.\" Let me check if the current method.py actually does this or not.\n\nLooking at current method.py: it computes `p1G = p1 @ G_exp` and `pmG = p_mix @ G_exp` — that's two full p@G matmuls. But we could compute it with just p0@G and p1@G plus a dot product, saving one `(B,H,L,L)` matmul.\n\nLet me also check if there's a way to further optimize. Let me also think about the case when `alpha == 1.0` — currently it short-circuits to just `p0 @ v`, but we still need the norm ratio. Wait no, when alpha=1, p1=p0, so u1=u0, m=u0, ratio=1.0. Actually the current code for alpha==1.0 is correct — it just returns `p0 @ v`. That's right because ratio=1 and m=u0, so r*m = u0, output = u0 @ wv^T = p0 @ v. Good.\n\nLet me benchmark the key insight: computing normm_sq from p0, p1 and their cross term instead of computing p_mix @ G separately.\n\nAlso, another thought: we can further optimize by fusing the `p1G * p1` sum with more efficient operations, and possibly by avoiding the full `p_mix` materialization (since we only need p_mix @ v and the norm, both can be computed from p0 and p1).\n\nLet me write a benchmark script to test several ideas:\n1. Compute normm_sq from p0G and p1G instead of p_mix @ G (saves 1 p@G matmul)\n2. Avoid materializing p_mix entirely (compute output as lerp of p0@v and p1@v)\n3. In-place operations where safe"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/bench_opt.py << 'PYEOF'\nimport math\nimport time\nimport torch\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\ndef ref_attention(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    q = torch.einsum(\\\"blc,hdc->bhld\\\", x, wq)\n    k = torch.einsum(\\\"blc,hdc->bhld\\\", x, wk)\n    logits = (q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)) / math.sqrt(wq.shape[1])\n    p0 = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\n    base = p0 @ x.unsqueeze(1)\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        modified = base\n    else:\n        perturbed = .5 * (1 + alpha) * logits + .5 * (1 - alpha) * logits.transpose(-1, -2)\n        modified = perturbed.softmax(dim=-1) @ x.unsqueeze(1)\n    blended = base + beta * (modified - base)\n    ratio = (modified.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)\n             / blended.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)).clamp(.25, 4.)\n    y = torch.einsum(\\\"bhlc,hdc->bhld\\\", blended * ratio, wv)\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\ndef current_best(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n    q = (xr @ wq.reshape(H * D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    k = (xr @ wk.reshape(H * D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    v = (xr @ wv.reshape(H * D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2) * inv_sqrt_d\n    p0 = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = p0 @ v\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n        p1 = (a_p * logits + a_m * logits.transpose(-1, -2)).softmax(dim=-1)\n        p_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\n\n        G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n        G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n        p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n        norm1_sq = (p1G * p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n        pmG = p_mix @ G_exp\n        normm_sq = (pmG * p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n        ratio = (norm1 / normm).clamp(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        y = (p_mix @ v) * ratio\n\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\ndef opt_no_pmix_matmul(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Compute normm_sq from p0G and p1G, saving one p@G matmul.\n    normm_sq = ||(1-b)*u0 + b*u1||\"'^2 = (1-b)''^2*||u0||''^2 + b''^2*||u1||''^2 + 2*(1-b)*b*<u0,u1>\n    <u0,u1> per row = sum_j (p0_j * (p1 @ G)_j) = (p0 * p1G).sum(-1)\n    \"\"\"\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n    q = (xr @ wq.reshape(H * D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    k = (xr @ wk.reshape(H * D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    v = (xr @ wv.reshape(H * D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2) * inv_sqrt_d\n    p0 = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = p0 @ v\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n        p1 = (a_p * logits + a_m * logits.transpose(-1, -2)).softmax(dim=-1)\n\n        G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n        G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n        # Only one p@G matmul for p1 + use p0G for cross term\n        p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n        p0G = p0 @ G_exp\n\n        norm1_sq = (p1G * p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        norm0_sq = (p0G * p0).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        cross = (p0G * p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)  # <u0, u1>\n\n        b1 = 1.0 - beta\n        normm_sq = b1 * b1 * norm0_sq + beta * beta * norm1_sq + 2.0 * b1 * beta * cross\n\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n        ratio = (norm1 / normm).clamp(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        # p_mix @ v = (1-beta)*p0@v + beta*p1@v (avoid materializing p_mix)\n        y = torch.lerp(p0 @ v, p1 @ v, beta) * ratio\n\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n\ndef bench_median(fn, n=11):\n    for _ in range(3):\n        fn()\n    times = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        fn()\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        times.append((t1 - t0) / 1e6)\n    return sorted(times)[len(times) // 2]\n\ncases = [\n    (1, 64, 512, 8, 64, 1.05, 5.0),\n    (1, 128, 640, 10, 64, 1.1, 4.0),\n    (1, 128, 1280, 20, 64, 1.15, 3.0),\n    (1, 256, 1280, 20, 64, 1.05, 7.5),\n    (1, 256, 640, 10, 64, 1.2, 5.0),\n    (2, 128, 512, 8, 64, 1.0, 5.0),\n]\n\nvariants = [\n    (\"ref\", ref_attention),\n    (\"current\", current_best),\n    (\"opt_no_pmix\", opt_no_pmix_matmul),\n]\n\ngeomean_opt = [1.0] * (len(variants) - 1)\n\nfor B, L, C, H, D, alpha, beta in cases:\n    torch.manual_seed(42)\n    x = torch.randn(B, L, C)\n    wq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    wk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    wv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    \n    case_label = f\"B{B}L{L}C{C}H{H}\"\n    \n    ref_out = ref_attention(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n    \n    times = []\n    for name, fn in variants:\n        ms = bench_median(lambda: fn(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta), n=11)\n        times.append(ms)\n        \n        if name != \"ref\":\n            out = fn(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n            diff = (out - ref_out).abs().max().item()\n            rel_max = ref_out.abs().max().item()\n            tol = 3e-5 + 3e-4 * rel_max\n            status = \"OK\" if diff <= tol else f\"FAIL ({diff:.2e} > {tol:.2e})\"\n            print(f\"  {name}: max_diff={diff:.2e} {status}\")\n    \n    print(f\"{case_label:20s}  \", end=\"\")\n    for t in times:\n        print(f\"{t:10.2f}ms \", end=\"\")\n    print(f\"  cur/ref={times[1]/times[0]:.3f}  opt/ref={times[2]/times[0]:.3f}\")\n    \n    if times[0] > 0:\n        for j in range(1, len(variants)):\n            geomean_opt[j-1] *= times[j] / times[0]\n\nprint(f\"'\"\\\\nGeometric mean ratio (vs ref):\\\")\nfor j in range(1, len(variants)):\n    print(f\\\"  {variants[j][0]:20s}: {geomean_opt[j-1]**(1/len(cases)):.4f}\\\")\nPYEOF\npython /tmp/bench_opt.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
